  "result": "88a: SULFOLOBUS MEDIUM (ANAEROBIC) (https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium88a.pdf)\nciteturn44view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium88a.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 30\nL0@P0: 88a: SULFOLOBUS MEDIUM (ANAEROBIC)\nL1@P0: (NH4)2SO4 1.30 g\nL2@P0: KH2PO4 0.28 g\nL3@P0: MgSO4 x 7 H2O 0.25 g\nL4@P0: CaCl2 x 2 H2O 0.07 g\nL5@P0: FeCl3 x 6 H2O 0.02 g\nL6@P0: Allen's trace element solution 10.00 ml\nL7@P0: Sulfur (powder) 10.00 g\nL8@P0: Yeast extract (OXOID) 0.50 g\nL9@P0: Na2S x 9 H2O 0.50 g\nL10@P0: Distilled water 1000.00 ml\nL11@P0: Dissolve ingredients (except sulfur, yeast extract and sulfide), adjust pH of the salt\nL12@P0: solution at room temperature to 4.0 using 1 N H2SO4 and sparge medium with 100% N2\nL13@P0: gas to make it anoxic. Dispense medium under same gas atmosphere into anoxic\nL14@P0: Hungate-type tubes or serum vials that contain already the appropriate amount of sulfur.\nL15@P0: Sterilize medium by heating cultivation vessels in a boiling water bath for 1 - 2 hours on\nL16@P0: each of 3 successive days. Add yeast extract and sulfide from sterile anoxic stock solutions\nL17@P0: prepared under 100% N2 gas. Prior to inoculation check pH and adjust to 4.0, if necessary.\nL18@P0: For DSM 2161, DSM 2162: Use 1.00 g/l yeast extract and adjust pH of medium to 5.5.\nL19@P0: Allen's trace element solution (from medium 88)\nL20@P0: MnCl2 x 4 H2O 180.00 mg\nL21@P0: Na2B4O7 x 10 H2O 450.00 mg\nL22@P0: ZnSO4 x 7 H2O 22.00 mg\nL23@P0: CuCl2 x 2 H2O 5.00 mg\nL24@P0: Na2MoO4 x 2 H2O 3.00 mg\nL25@P0: VOSO4 x 2 H2O 3.00 mg\nL26@P0: CoSO4 x 7 H2O 1.00 mg\nL27@P0: Distilled water 1000.00 ml\nL28@P0: Adjust pH of final solution to 2 with 1 N HCl.\nL29@P0: © 2022 DSMZ - All rights reserved Page 1 of 1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium88b.pdf)\nciteturn44view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium88b.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 12\nL0@P0: © 2007 DSMZ GmbH - All rights reserved\nL1@P0: 88b. V24N MEDIUM\nL2@P0: Prepare medium 88 without yeast extract, then add (per litre):\nL3@P0: Sulfur, powdered 1.0 g\nL4@P0: Yeast extract 0.2 g\nL5@P0: Starch, soluble 2.0 g\nL6@P0: Resazurin 0.4 mg\nL7@P0: Na2S x 9 H2O 0.5 g\nL8@P0: Adjust the pH to 6.0 with H2SO4 (25% v/v). Prepare the medium under 100% N2 gas\nL9@P0: phase and distribute anaerobically into rubber stoppered tubes or bottles (presterilized\nL10@P0: by autoclaving). The medium is sterilized by heating 2 hours at 85 C on each of two\nL11@P0: following days.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n88c: ZESTOSPHAERA MEDIUM (https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium88c.pdf)\nciteturn44view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last year; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium88c.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 30\nL0@P0: 88c: ZESTOSPHAERA MEDIUM\nL1@P0: (NH4)2SO4 1.30 g\nL2@P0: KH2PO4 0.28 g\nL3@P0: MgSO4 x 7 H2O 0.25 g\nL4@P0: CaCl2 x 2 H2O 0.07 g\nL5@P0: FeCl3 x 6 H2O 0.02 g\nL6@P0: Allen's trace element solution 10.00 ml\nL7@P0: Na2S2O3 x 5 H2O 2.00 g\nL8@P0: Yeast extract (OXOID) 1.00 g\nL9@P0: Tryptone peptone (Bacto BD) 1.00 g\nL10@P0: Casamino acids (Difco BD) 0.50 g\nL11@P0: Na2S x 9 H2O 0.50 g\nL12@P0: Distilled water 1000.00 ml\nL13@P0: Dissolve ingredients (except thiosulfate, yeast extract, Tryptone, Casamino acids and\nL14@P0: sulfide), sparge medium with 80% N2 and 20% CO2 gas mixture to make it anoxic and\nL15@P0: dispense medium under same gas atmosphere into serum bottels. After autoclaving add\nL16@P0: thiosulfate, yeast extract, Tryptone, Casamino acids and sulfide from sterile anoxic stock\nL17@P0: solutions prepared under 100% N2 gas. Prior to inoculation check pH and adjust to 6.0, if\nL18@P0: necessary.\nL19@P0: Allen's trace element solution (from medium 88)\nL20@P0: MnCl2 x 4 H2O 180.00 mg\nL21@P0: Na2B4O7 x 10 H2O 450.00 mg\nL22@P0: ZnSO4 x 7 H2O 22.00 mg\nL23@P0: CuCl2 x 2 H2O 5.00 mg\nL24@P0: Na2MoO4 x 2 H2O 3.00 mg\nL25@P0: VOSO4 x 2 H2O 3.00 mg\nL26@P0: CoSO4 x 7 H2O 1.00 mg\nL27@P0: Distilled water 1000.00 ml\nL28@P0: Adjust pH of final solution to 2 with 1 N HCl.\nL29@P0: © 2022 DSMZ - All rights reserved Page 1 of 1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n358a: ACIDIANUS MEDIUM (ANAEROBIC) (https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium358a.pdf)\nciteturn44view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 2; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium358a.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 39\nL0@P0: 358a: ACIDIANUS MEDIUM (ANAEROBIC)\nL1@P0: (NH4)2SO4 1.30 g\nL2@P0: KH2PO4 0.28 g\nL3@P0: MgSO4 x 7 H2O 0.25 g\nL4@P0: CaCl2 x 2 H2O 0.07 g\nL5@P0: FeCl3 x 6 H2O 0.02 g\nL6@P0: Allen's trace element solution 10.00 ml\nL7@P0: Sulfur (powder) 5.00 g\nL8@P0: Yeast extract (OXOID) 0.50 g\nL9@P0: Distilled water 1000.00 ml\nL10@P0: 1. Dissolve ingredients, except sulfur and yeast extract, bring medium to the boil, then\nL11@P0: cool to room temperature under 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas mixture and adjust pH to 2.5\nL12@P0: using 10 N H2SO4. Dispense medium under same gas atmosphere into anoxic\nL13@P0: Hungate-type tubes or serum vials (e.g., 20 ml medium in 100 ml serum bottles)\nL14@P0: containing already the appropriate amount of sulfur. For sterilization sealed bottles with\nL15@P0: medium are heated in a boiling water bath for 2 - 3 h on each of 3 successive days. Add\nL16@P0: yeast extract from a sterile anoxic stock solution prepared under 100% N2 gas\nL17@P0: atmosphere.\nL18@P0: 2. Pressurize inoculated bottles to 1 bar overpressure with sterile 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas\nL19@P0: mixture.\nL20@P0: 3. Note: Inoculate with 5% (w/v) culture. Incubate without shaking.\nL21@P0: For DSM 3772: Reduce amount of yeast extract to 0.02 g/l.\nL22@P0: For DSM 6296: Reduce amount of yeast extract to 0.20 g/l and adjust pH to 2.5 - 3.0.\nL23@P0: Pressurize inoculated bottles to 2 bar overpressure with sterile 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas\nL24@P0: mixture.\nL25@P0: For DSM 6334: Reduce amount of yeast extract to 0.20 g/l. Pressurize inoculated bottles to\nL26@P0: 2 bar overpressure with sterile 80% H2 and 20% CO2 gas mixture.\nL27@P0: Allen's trace element solution (from medium 88)\nL28@P0: MnCl2 x 4 H2O 180.00 mg\nL29@P0: Na2B4O7 x 10 H2O 450.00 mg\nL30@P0: ZnSO4 x 7 H2O 22.00 mg\nL31@P0: CuCl2 x 2 H2O 5.00 mg\nL32@P0: Na2MoO4 x 2 H2O 3.00 mg\nL33@P0: VOSO4 x 2 H2O 3.00 mg\nL34@P0: CoSO4 x 7 H2O 1.00 mg\nL35@P0: Distilled water 1000.00 ml\nL36@P0-1: © 2022 DSMZ - All rights reserved Page 1 of 2358a: ACIDIANUS MEDIUM (ANAEROBIC)\nL37@P1: Adjust pH of final solution to 2 with 1 N HCl.\nL38@P1: © 2022 DSMZ - All rights reserved Page 2 of 2\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium600a.pdf)\nciteturn44view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last year; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium600a.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 36\nL0@P0: © 2007 DSMZ GmbH - All rights reserved\nL1@P0: 600a. M13a (PIRELLULA) MEDIUM\nL2@P0: Peptone 0.25 g\nL3@P0: Yeast extract 0.25 g\nL4@P0: Glucose 0.25 g\nL5@P0: Vitamin solution (see below) 10.0 ml\nL6@P0: Hutner's basal salts\nL7@P0: (see medium 590) 20.0 ml\nL8@P0: 0.1 M Tris/HCl buffer pH 7.5 50.0 ml\nL9@P0: Artifical sea water 500.0 ml\nL10@P0: Distilled water 420.0 ml\nL11@P0: Vitamin solution:\nL12@P0: Vitamin B12 0.2 mg\nL13@P0: Biotin 4.0 mg\nL14@P0: Thiamine-HCl x 2 H2O 10.0 mg\nL15@P0: Ca-pantothenate 10.0 mg\nL16@P0: Folic acid 1.0 mg\nL17@P0: Riboflavin 10.0 mg\nL18@P0: Nicotinamide 10.0 mg\nL19@P0: p-Aminobenzoic acid 10.0 mg\nL20@P0: Pyridoxine hydrochloride 10.0 mg\nL21@P0: Distilled water 1000.0 ml\nL22@P0: Filter-sterilized.\nL23@P0: Artifical sea water:\nL24@P0: NaCl 23.47 g\nL25@P0: Na2SO4 3.92 g\nL26@P0: MgCl2 x 6 H2O 4.98 g\nL27@P0: CaCl2 1.10 g\nL28@P0: NaHCO3 192.0 mg\nL29@P0: KCl 664.0 mg\nL30@P0: KBr 96.0 mg\nL31@P0: H3BO3 26.0 mg\nL32@P0: SrCl2 24.0 mg\nL33@P0: NaF 3.0 mg\nL34@P0: Distilled water 1000.0 ml\nL35@P0: For agar plates increase the pH of the Tris/HCl buffer to 8.5.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium600b.pdf)\nciteturn44view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium600b.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 35\nL0@P0: © 2012 DSMZ GmbH - All rights reserved\nL1@P0: 600b. M13 (3x) PIRELLULA MEDIUM\nL2@P0: Peptone 0.75 g\nL3@P0: Yeast extract 0.75 g\nL4@P0: Glucose 0.75 g\nL5@P0: Vitamin solution No.6 10.0 ml\nL6@P0: Hutner's basal salts (see medium 590) 20.0 ml\nL7@P0: 0.1 M Tris/HCl buffer pH 7.5 50.0 ml\nL8@P0: Artifical sea water 250.0 ml\nL9@P0: Distilled water 720.0 ml\nL10@P0: Vitamin solution No.6:\nL11@P0: Vitamin B12 0.2 mg\nL12@P0: Biotin 4.0 mg\nL13@P0: Thiamine-HCl x 2 H2O 10.0 mg\nL14@P0: Ca-pantothenate 10.0 mg\nL15@P0: Folic acid 1.0 mg\nL16@P0: Riboflavin 10.0 mg\nL17@P0: Nicotinamide 10.0 mg\nL18@P0: p-Aminobenzoic acid 10.0 mg\nL19@P0: Pyridoxine hydrochloride 10.0 mg\nL20@P0: Distilled water 1000.0 ml\nL21@P0: Filter-sterilized.\nL22@P0: Artifical sea water:\nL23@P0: NaCl 23.47 g\nL24@P0: Na2SO4 3.92 g\nL25@P0: MgCl2 x 6 H2O 10.64 g\nL26@P0: CaCl2 1.10 g\nL27@P0: NaHCO3 192.00 mg\nL28@P0: KCl 664.00 mg\nL29@P0: KBr 96.00 mg\nL30@P0: H3BO3 26.00 mg\nL31@P0: SrCl2 24.00 mg\nL32@P0: NaF 3.00 mg\nL33@P0: Distilled water 1000.00 ml\nL34@P0: For agar plates increase the pH of the Tris/HCl buffer to 8.5.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium607a.pdf)\nciteturn44view6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium607a.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 4\nL0@P0: © 2007 DSMZ GmbH - All rights reserved\nL1@P0: 607a. FILOBACILLUS MILOSENSIS MEDIUM\nL2@P0: Use medium 607 with modification peptone, yeast extract and glucose in triple\nL3@P0: concentration each; (0.75 g/l instead of 0.25 g/l); 10% NaCl is added (w/v).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1060 (https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium1560a.pdf)\nciteturn44view7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 7 months ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 2; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium1560a.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 73\nL0@P0: © 2009 DSMZ GmbH - All rights reserved\nL1@P0: 1560a. PLANCTOMYCES MEDIUM WITH DOUBLE CONCENTRATED\nL2@P0:  ARTIFICAL SEA WATER\nL3@P0: Peptone (Bacto) 0.25 g\nL4@P0: Yeast extract (Bacto) 0.25 g\nL5@P0: HEPES 2.38 g\nL6@P0: Mineral salt solution (see below) 20.00 ml\nL7@P0: Trace element solution (see below) 1.00 ml\nL8@P0: Artifical sea water (see below) 250.00 ml\nL9@P0: Agar (Bacto) 15.00 g\nL10@P0: Double distilled water 730.00 ml\nL11@P0: Sterilize 20 min./121C. After cooling to 60C add:\nL12@P0: N-Acetylglucosamine (20g/L stock solution) 40.0 ml\nL13@P0: Glucose sol. (2.5%, sterile-filtered) 10.0 ml\nL14@P0: Vitamin sol. (double conc.)(see below) 5.0 ml\nL15@P0: Adjust pH to 7.5 (the medium is only weakly buffered; one needs approx. 10 drops/l\nL16@P0: medium of 6 N KOH).\nL17@P0: Artifical sea water:\nL18@P0: NaCl 93.88 g\nL19@P0: Na2SO4 15.68 g\nL20@P0: MgCl2 x 6 H2O 42.56 g\nL21@P0: CaCl2 5.72 g\nL22@P0: NaHCO3 0.76 g\nL23@P0: KCl 2.76 g\nL24@P0: KBr 0.38 g\nL25@P0: H3BO3 0.10 g\nL26@P0: SrCl2 0.16 g\nL27@P0: NaF 0.012 g\nL28@P0: Double distilled water 1000.000 ml\nL29@P0: Mineral salts solution:\nL30@P0: Nitrilotriacetic acid (NTA) 10.00 g\nL31@P0: MgSO4 x 7 H20 29.70 g\nL32@P0: CaCl2 x 2 H2O 3.34 g\nL33@P0: Na2MoO7O4 x 2 H2O 12.67 mg\nL34@P0: FeSO4 x 7 H2O 99.00 mg\nL35@P0: “Metals 44” (see below) 50.00 ml\nL36@P0: Distilled water 950.00 ml\nL37@P0: Dissolve the nitrilotriacetic acid, adjust the pH to 7.0 with KOH (about 7.3 g). Dissolve\nL38@P0-1: other salts separately, combine and adjust the pH to 6.8 with NaOH or H2SO4.© 2009 DSMZ GmbH - All rights reserved\nL39@P1: \"Metals 44\":\nL40@P1: Na-EDTA 250.000 mg\nL41@P1: ZnSO4 x 7 H2O 1095.000 mg\nL42@P1: FeSO4 x 7 H2O 500.000 mg\nL43@P1: MnSO4 x H2O 154.000 mg\nL44@P1: CuSO4 x 5 H2O 39.200 mg\nL45@P1: Co(NO3)2 x 6 H2O 24.800 mg\nL46@P1: Na2B4O7 x 10 H2O 17.700 mg\nL47@P1: Distilled water 1000.000 ml\nL48@P1: Trace element solution:\nL49@P1: Na-Nitrilotriacetat 1.50 g\nL50@P1: MnSO4 x H2O 0.50 g\nL51@P1: Fe SO4 x 7 H2O 0.10 g\nL52@P1: Co(NO3)2 x 6 H2O 0.10 g\nL53@P1: ZnCl2 0.10 g\nL54@P1: NiCl2 x 6 H2O 0.05 g\nL55@P1: H2SeO3 0.05 g\nL56@P1: CuSO4 x 5 H2O 0.01 g\nL57@P1: AlK(SO4)2 x 12 H2O 0.01 g\nL58@P1: H3BO3 0.01 g\nL59@P1: Na2MoO4 x 2 H2O 0.01 g\nL60@P1: Na2WO4 x 2 H2O 0.01 g\nL61@P1: Double distilled water 1000.00 ml\nL62@P1: Vitamin solution (double conc.):\nL63@P1: Biotin 4.00 mg\nL64@P1: Folic acid 4.00 mg\nL65@P1: Pyridoxine-HCl 20.00 mg\nL66@P1: Riboflavine 10.00 mg\nL67@P1: Thiamine-HCl x 2 H2O 10.00 mg\nL68@P1: Nicotinamide 10.00 mg\nL69@P1: D-Ca-pantothenate 10.00 mg\nL70@P1: Vitamin B12 0.20 mg\nL71@P1: p-Aminobenzoic acid 10.00 mg\nL72@P1: Double distil